sessions.summary:
Steps 1–10 are implemented. `npm test` passes (20 tests) and `npm run build` finishes without error. I could not run `npm run dev` or play the game in a browser, so the rendering, controls, UI and save/continue flow are untested beyond compiling.

- **Starting point:** the skeleton only had signatures, so I wrote all of `src/engine/` myself.
- **Engine tests:** I added `test/engine-extra.test.js` for the edge cases. It covers:
  - noise continuity;
  - terrain rules and one coal ore per chunk;
  - 1-block versus 2-block jump;
  - sneak at an edge;
  - raycast edge cases;
  - mesh winding and culling;
  - shifted crafting recipes;
  - serialization.
- **Engine contract:** `src/engine/` imports no three, react or DOM, and uses no `Math.random` or `Date`. I also added `src/engine/atlas.js` (tile layout and UV) and `getChunkData` in `world.js`, which bakes edits into the cached chunk arrays. The mesher reads those arrays and the four neighbouring chunks directly.
- **Render (`src/render/`):**
  - Textures: atlas, item icons and 10 crack stages, all generated in code.
  - Sky: day/night colours, sun, moon, lights and fog.
  - `ChunkManager`: loads and unloads chunks with a time budget per frame, queues edits first, and disposes geometries.
  - `GameRenderer`: scene, camera, target outline and crack overlay.
- **Game logic (`src/game/`):** `GameController` has no React in it. It handles:
  - pointer lock, with pause driven by `pointerlockchange`;
  - preventDefault on F3, Space, Ctrl, the mouse wheel and right-click;
  - double-tap W to sprint;
  - mining with crack progress, placing, middle-click pick, and right-click on a crafting table to open the 3x3 screen;
  - a 30-second autosave and save on pause.

  `invScreen.js` holds the held stack and crafting grid, and returns them to the inventory on close and before saving. `save.js` validates the save on load and falls back to the menu if it is corrupt.
- **UI (`src/ui/`):** main menu, HUD with hotbar and item name, inventory screen (2x2 or 3x3 crafting), pause menu, F3 debug overlay, `App.jsx` and `styles.css`. `main.jsx` renders the app without StrictMode, so the pointer-lock and autosave side effects don't run twice.

I did not call the advisor.
